      "writtenOn": "2024-06-06T17:11:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can simplify this by just treating `desc` as a span of uint32_t\u0027s (which could either be a helper added to SamplerDesc, or could be declaring a fixed-size uint32_t array here and memcpy\u0027ing desc into it).\n\nIf we want to keep the variable size of the sampler desc data, we can avoid the dynamic allocation of `samplerData` because we know the max size of the span already (3 uint32_t\u0027s), and then we just adjust the size of the span based on `usesExternalFormat()`.\n\n3 uints vs 2 uints isn\u0027t that different for fairly uncommonly used textures (and will likely be textures that are used in a simple shader so the rest of the key will be pretty small). I think then the simplicity of just copying in and out the SamplerDesc is better since the serialization and deserialization is handled in very different parts of the code.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 71,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 76,
        "endChar": 41
      },
      "revId": "54d5d2a33f3829911500a9a869b06397da0623f4",
