      "writtenOn": "2024-06-12T02:22:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, I agree this could be handled better, but it gets a little wonky considering that the external format MSBs value (when present/real) is sandwiched between the two values that are always present. So instead of getting a subspan or just chopping off the last value, we would just want samplerData[0] and samplerData[2].\n\nFor this latest patch I\u0027ve made the external format MSBs be appended at the end and gone with your `memcpy` suggestion, simply chopping off the last value if we are using a known format. LMKWYT!",
